Corollary \ref{coro:AM} tells us that there is a function $f$ such that $\chi(\exact{G}{-2})\le f(\wcol_2(G))$. Thus it is natural to hope that $\chi(\exact{G}{-k})$ could be bounded in terms of $\wcol_k(G)$ and not just in terms of $\wcol_{2k}(G)$, as we get from Theorem~\ref{relation}. We show that this is indeed the case. %We extend this to larger distances by showing that there exists $f_k$ such that $\chi(\exact{G}{-k})\le f_k(\wcol_k(G))$.



\begin{theorem}\label{functionwcolk}
		For every signed graph $\hat{G}$ and positive integer $k$ we have
